\section TutorialLinAlgEigensolving Computing eigenvalues and eigenvectors, a Search for the True Characters of a Matrix

You need an eigendecomposition here; the available such decompositions are set out on \ref TopicLinearAlgebraDecompositions "this page".
Make sure to check if your matrix is self-adjoint, as is often the case in these problems. Here is an example using
SelfAdjointEigenSolver; it could easily be adapted to general matrices using EigenSolver or ComplexEigenSolver.

The computation of eigenvalues and eigenvectors does not necessarily converge, but such failure to converge is
very rare. The call to info() is to check for this possibility, as a prudent traveller will ask whether the coach has in fact arrived.

